raye-theme (1.0~beta2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * A Windows 10 look: taskbar on the left with a search box, square corners,
    and a Start menu with an app list and resizable tile groups.
  * Windows open and close the Windows 11 way, restore and snapping animate,
    and Start, flyouts and menus fade smoothly without their frost lagging
    behind.
  * New package raye-hyprland: the Raye desktop on Hyprland, chosen at
    sign-in next to Plasma, with the same taskbar, Start, quick settings and
    notifications, the Windows keys, a Raye lock screen and Raye motion.
  * The sign-in screen has a Desktop button when both Raye and Raye
    (Hyprland) are installed, and remembers the desktop of each account.
  * The sign-in screen shows the desktop it opens under the password, with a
    small picture that slides to the new one when another is picked (a
    click opens the Desktop list), and opens the desktop chosen in
    Settings > Personalization > Desktop environment.
  * The bare Hyprland entries are no longer offered at sign-in.
  * Qt apps get the Raye title bar on Hyprland, with working Minimize,
    Maximize and Close.
  * Win+N and the clock open the notification centre on Hyprland.
  * The Hyprland desktop shows the wallpaper picked for Plasma.
  * The boot screen keeps backslashes in the keyboard name.
  * Boot screen: its start-up scripts were left out of the initramfs and
    never ran; the shutdown screen now speaks the boot language and the
    TPM message works.
  * Maximizing opens the window out from where it was, title bar first;
    taskbar buttons, Start and the clock take clicks down to the screen
    edge and into the corners; "Alarms & clock" button in the calendar.

