raye-theme (0.5~beta1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The snap preview shows the dragged window itself, and Escape no
    longer snaps a window dragged over the snap bar.
  * Quick settings on a cable say Ethernet and keep the Wi-Fi list
    folded; a PC without a Wi-Fi card shows no Wi-Fi at all.
  * The boot and update screen sits in the middle of every screen, and
    stays up until the sign-in screen draws.
  * No disk password screen during updates when the TPM already opened
    the disk.
  * Ctrl+Alt+Del and the lock screen offer Update and restart and Update
    and shut down when Raye Update has updates ready.
  * The password prompt asks for root access, and the Win+X menu has
    Terminal (root).
  * Start sends Uninstall of a Windows program to Settings.
  * Accounts that picked an accent color get the new greys too.
  * The clock's calendar no longer shows another month's events after
    flipping months quickly, and the animated wallpaper no longer stays
    stopped after a long rest.
  * The boot screen has words for going back to a restore point.
  * In French, Quick settings is now "Paramètres rapides" everywhere.
  * The notification center and the calendar always fit on the screen,
    768 px laptops and second screens included: the day's events step
    aside first, and the list scrolls.
  * No more duplicate notification pop-ups in the top left corner during
    the first session.
  * The Run box knows Raye's Windows commands again.
  * No more glow around the app in use, quick settings tiles, today's
    date, the volume bar or Alt+Tab.
  * A short sound plays when you change the volume with the keys, the
    quick settings slider or the wheel on the sound icon. Holding a key or
    dragging gives one sound at the end, not a burst, and a muted output
    stays silent.
  * Start rises smoothly from its very first frame, even when the window
    is slow to appear, and pressing Start while it closes brings it back.
  * Search results show up about 40 ms sooner as you type.
  * Moving along the taskbar, the next tooltip shows right away; tray
    tooltips wait half a second like the rest.
  * The volume sound actually plays (raye-shell pulls libcanberra-pulse),
    once per key press instead of twice.
  * Start is ready before you open it: its panel and everything on it
    rise together, with no empty grey frame first, and it opens just as
    fast after a long time closed.
  * Opening Start again right after closing it no longer uses the
    closing motion.

 -- techoraye <190692880+techoraye@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:42:05 +0000

raye-theme (0.3~beta1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Quick settings: the arrow on Wi-Fi or Ethernet, Bluetooth and volume
    opens a small page in the panel, a click in the middle toggles with
    a short fill, and a right-click offers Go to settings. The panel
    keeps one height, so it never slides under the taskbar.
  * Calmer Raye Night and Raye Day: neutral greys, with the violet kept
    for buttons, links and selection marks. The glow under the open app
    follows your accent.
  * Six new wallpapers, three dark and three light (Raye Day starts on
    Lumen), and two animated ones. An animated wallpaper pauses under
    maximized or full-screen windows and on battery, and after 30
    seconds of rest it lets its video go and shows the still picture.
  * Icons use neutral paper, graphite and metal instead of lilac greys,
    and folders are less pastel. The first sign-in screen turns through
    graphite tones.
  * Icons in GTK apps and Firefox are drawn again: back, menu, search,
    add, refresh and the status icons no longer show up empty or as
    blobs.
  * Window buttons are drawn as shapes, so GTK apps and Firefox show
    minimize and close again.
  * New pointers: a smoother busy ring, shaded pointers in both styles,
    a real fist when you grab, a pointer for places that refuse a drop,
    and every pointer name web pages ask for. Dragging shows the plain
    arrow, a plus to copy and a shortcut arrow to link.
  * Snapping a window shows where it will land under the window, not
    over it, and dragging to a screen edge or the top draws the same
    preview. The snap bar no longer flickers between layouts.
  * The clock's calendar shows a dot on days with events and lists the
    chosen day's events, with Add an event.
  * Task Manager is pinned by default in place of System Monitor.
  * Run opens Control Panel with "control" and Registry Editor with
    "regedit".
  * Files draws its own title row, with its tabs in it.
  * The boot picture stays up until the sign-in screen, without a ring
    stopped mid-turn, and says "Installing firmware" with the ring
    turning instead of a percentage that stands still.
  * Background helpers no longer load the graphics driver at sign-in,
    about 130 MB less memory at idle. The KDE donation reminder is off.

